{"title":"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db68e8a2aef3038cdc7576a07fba22e4de36d0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2278d67dcf2c3f9a73967961071ed4672ca776ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\phi(n)&gt;n-\\sqrt{n},\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edae70ddedf89e790936ed4035c5ca1480212e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the number of integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02ceb79ec6bdbd59db7f370e2ab457c332683cba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(n) &gt; n - \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"22\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is prime or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><b>IF:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is prime, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d055919b114f3d6510338f69f116ba0f853fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(n) = n - 1 &gt; n - \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"22\" />, which is true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> the statement is true as well.\n</p><p><b>ONLY IF:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not prime and not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must have a prime divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517602127c63a45b75fb3ced3cfed9ed5a3e1741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\leq \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"21\" />; if this was not the case, then the number of not necessarily distinct prime factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> could have must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, contradiction. It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba2ffc0b37409be8d1665c00ce51ff11ecd68fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\phi(n) \\leq \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{p} \\right) \\cdot n \\leq \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\right) \\cdot n = n - \\sqrt{n}.\\]\" width=\"377\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>This proves both directions of the claim. All that remains is to sum the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> prime numbers and add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to obtain an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943f1bb3c45c168510d5c5393c96778d85511e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{964}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041032\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 84/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4137/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21802:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041032 and revision id 159736. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}